
ms.c : Mergesort - uses fork and does the two parts using child/parent
        Note - lots of stuff is commented out - making it sequential
	You may want to copy it to par.c and then remove those comments between /* ... */  to make it parallel

	See how fork and exec are used. 
	See relationship of parallel code to the sequential code

	Put some sleeps (1) before child returns  (2) before main calls mergesort
	In another window see the pstree

 Additionally, you can 
		readelf -W -a a.out 
	to see the sections segments, their mappings and program headers

	See the difference between -static and the default dynamic
		the sections .symtba and .string
		the sections .dynsym and .dynstr

dgen.sh : A bash script to generate a large input to ms.c
